From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] media: mediatek: camsv: add the MT6878 MM M4U camera
 client

The MT6878 MM M4U runs under the vendor hypervisor's hyp-mmu type2: the
hypervisor shadows the kernel's ARMv7s table, the PT base register reads
back the hypervisor's table, and every change to the table has to be
followed by HYP_PMM_HYPMMU_TYPE2_INV. The camera larbs boot with MMU_EN=1
and CAMSV issues no memory transactions until the M4U is set up.

Set the M4U up the way the stock mtk_iommu and iommu_secure modules do:
hw_init including the TF-A secure bank init call (MTK_SIP 0x514, MM
IOMMU 0, bank 4), the PT base once per boot, then per map or unmap a
type2 invalidate and a range TLB flush. No global invalidate is issued.
Bank 0 is shared with the display, whose larbs must stay in bypass; this
is checked before first use.

A second PT base write in the same boot hangs the MM bus, so the table
lives until reboot and the module cannot be unloaded.
